<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Tanganyika Territory</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1961 CE · capital Dar es Salaam</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British-ruled mandate that replaced German East Africa on the mainland of Tanzania and became independent under Julius Nyerere in 1961.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>British forces conquered most of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. In 1920 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> set up a civil administration, and in 1922 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> confirmed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tanganyika">Tanganyika</a> as a British mandate, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dar-es-salaam">Dar es Salaam</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it became a UN trust territory.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donald-cameron-colonial-administrator">Donald Cameron</a> introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a> through chiefs and native authorities from 1925. The economy rested on sisal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, with settler estates in the north. After 1945 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groundnut">Groundnut</a> Scheme, a vast plan to grow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peanut">peanuts</a>, collapsed at great cost. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> spread as a common language, aiding national politics. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-african-national-union">TANU</a>, founded in 1954 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a>, won the elections of 1958 to 1960.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tanganyika">Tanganyika</a> became independent on 9 December 1961 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Nyerere</a> and a republic a year later. In 1964 it united with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a> to form <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tanzania">Tanzania</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tanganyika-territory.jpg" alt="Tanganyika Territory" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tanganyika_(1923%E2%80%931961).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1961 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dar es Salaam</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Donald Cameron, Richard Turnbull</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, Islam, traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swahili, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tanzania">Tanzania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Tanganyika, Tanganyika Mandate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1940&amp;focus=tanganyika-territory" aria-label="Tanganyika Territory on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5767 2432 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tanganyika Territory lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6087 2688L5857 2500M6087 2688L6087 2688M6087 2688L4997 651M6087 2688L6087 2688"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5857 2500h0M6087 2688h0M4997 651h0M6087 2688h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6087 2688h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6087 2688h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dar es Salaam. <a href="/atlas?year=1940&amp;focus=tanganyika-territory">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
